d.leftVal} < 0\\`)? **Yes, True!** Because \\`c\\` is negative (\\`${cond.leftVal}\\`), Python goes inside this \\`if\\` block to reset \\`c\\` back to \\`0\\`.`\n294:           : `We ask: Is \\`c < 0\\` (\\`Is ${cond.leftVal} < 0\\`)? **No, False.** Since \\`${cond.leftVal}\\` is not negative, we do not reset \\`c\\`—we keep this sum for the next number!`;\n295:       } else {\n296:         explanation = `We test \\`${cond.expr}\\` by comparing \\`${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}\\`, which is **${cond.result ? \"True\" : \"False\"}**.`;\n297:       }\n298: \n299:       return {\n300:         title: stepTitle,\n301:         calculationCard: {\n302:           currentNumber: null,\n303:           before: `${cond.leftExpr} is ${cond.leftVal}, ${cond.rightExpr} is ${cond.rightVal}`,\n304:           calculation: `${cond.leftVal} ${cond.operator} ${cond.rightVal}`,\n305:           after: cond.result ? \"True (Run the indented line)\" : \"False (Skip the indented line)\"\n306:         },\n307:         whatItMeans: explanation,\n308:         variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n309:         whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n310:         finalBanner: null\n311:       };\n312:     }\n313: \n314:     // 9. Return Statement\n315:     if (step.eventType === \"RETURN\") {\n316:       const subText =\n317:         bestSubarrayInfo && bestSubarrayInfo.subarray\n318:           ? `The continuous section \\`[${bestSubarrayInfo.subarray.join(\", \")}]\\` has the largest sum: **${op.returnVal}**.`\n319:           : `The function finishes and returns the final answer: **${op.returnVal}**.`;\n320: \n321:       return {\n322:         title: `Step ${n}: Return the final answer (${op.returnVal})`,\n323:         calculationCard: null,\n324:         whatItMeans:\n325:           `We have finished checking the entire list! \\`return ans\\` sends our final largest sum **\\`${op.returnVal}\\`** back as the answer.`,\n326:         variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n327:         whatHappensNext: `The program is complete! You can click Restart or try a different list of numbers above.`,\n328:         finalBanner: {\n329:           answer: op.returnVal,\n330:           summary: subText\n331:         }\n332:       };\n333:     }\n334: \n335:     // Fallback for print / break / continue / exceptions\n336:     return {\n337:       title: `Step ${n}: Execute line ${step.line}`,\n338:       calculationCard: null,\n339:       whatItMeans:\n340:         step.eventType === \"PRINT\"\n341:           ? `Python displays \\`\"${op.output}\"\\` as output.`\n342:           : step.eventType === \"EXCEPTION\"\n343:           ? `Python stopped with an error: \\`${op.message}\\`.`\n344:           : `Python runs \\`${step.codeText}\\`.`,\n345:       variableValuesNow: relevantVarsNow,\n346:       whatHappensNext: nextSentence,\n347:       finalBanner: null\n348:     };\n349:   }\n350: \n351:   formatRelevantVariablesNow(step) {\n352:     const vars = step.variables || [];\n353:     // Filter out large `nums` list from the inline text summary so it focuses on `c`, `ans`, `i`, etc.\n354:     const compact = vars.filter((v) => v.name !== \"nums\");\n355:     if (compact.length === 0) {\n356:       if (vars.length > 0) {\n357:         return vars.map((v) => `${v.name} = ${v.current}`).join(\", \");\n358:       }\n359:       return \"No variables created yet\";\n360:     }\n361:     const parts = compact.map((v) => `${v.name} = ${v.current}`);\n362:     if (step.loop && step.loop.indexedElementInfo) {\n363:       const el = step.loop.indexedElementInfo;\n364:       parts.push(`${el.arrayName}[${el.indexVal}] = ${el.elementVal}`);\n365:     }\n366:     return parts.join(\"   •   \");\n367:   }\n368: \n369:   buildFriendlyWhatNext(step, nextStep) {\n370:     if (!nextStep) {\n371:       return \"We have reached the end of the program!\";\n372:     }\n373:     const nextCode = nextStep.codeText || \"\";\n374:     if (nextStep.eventType === \"METHOD_DEF\" || nextStep.event