{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T11:28:01Z","input_tokens":10415,"cache_read_tokens":94130,"output_tokens":9795,"thinking":"Begin creating the necessary files within the specified build directory. First, reviewing the file list to ensure accurate file generation.\n\n\nInitial file list confirms the directory structure's validity. Now considering the need to synchronize root files with the `app_build` directory, and the implications for the server's behavior. The synchronization strategy needs to accommodate potential caching issues with browser and ensure that changes in root files reflect correctly.\n\n\nThe current server setup allows for simultaneous serving from the root and build directories based on restart timing. Need to ensure seamless transitions regardless of refresh timing. Updating server code to use the build directory and matching root static files with the build, will ensure a consistent experience.\n\n\nFocusing on constructing the `engine.py` to support both standalone functions and class-based solutions is the first priority. Implementing the AST-based expression stepper with short-circuit evaluation for boolean operations is crucial. Initial implementation will prioritize functionality and address edge cases in subsequent iterations.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\napp_build — Isolated Application Source Package for Code Flow Visualizer\nContains the Thonny-style Python execution tracer, sub-expression evaluator,\nstack/heap reference model tracker, and rule-based explanation engine.\n\"\"\"\n","Description":"Create app_build/__init__.py package initializer","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\app_build\\__init__.py","toolAction":"Creating app_build/__init__.py","toolSummary":"Create app_build/__init__.py"}},{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\napp_build/engine.py — Thonny-Style Python Execution Tracing Engine\nNo AI APIs. Uses Python's `ast` module and `sys.settrace` in a restricted sandbox.\nIncludes:\n1. Visual Reference Model (Name -> @Address -> Value Stack & Heap Memory Tracker)\n2. Step-by-Step Sub-Expression Evaluator with Short-Circuit ('and' / 'or') Handling\n3. Global vs. Local Variable Scope Isolation across the call stack\n4. Visual Garbage Collection (Reference counting & unreferenced heap object tracking)\n\"\"\"\n\nimport ast\nimport builtins\nimport copy\nimport io\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nSUPPORTED_BUILTINS = {\n    \"__build_class__\": builtins.__build_class__,\n    \"__name__\": \"__main__\",\n    \"object\": object,\n    \"abs\": abs,\n    \"bool\": bool,\n    \"dict\": dict,\n    \"enumerate\": enumerate,\n    \"float\": float,\n    \"int\": int,\n    \"len\": len,\n    \"list\": list,\n    \"max\": max,\n    \"min\": min,\n    \"print\": print,\n    \"range\": range,\n    \"round\": round,\n    \"set\": set,\n    \"sorted\": sorted,\n    \"str\": str,\n    \"sum\": sum,\n    \"tuple\": tuple,\n    \"zip\": zip,\n    \"True\": True,\n    \"False\": False,\n    \"None\": None,\n    \"Exception\": Exception,\n    \"IndexError\": IndexError,\n    \"ValueError\": ValueError,\n    \"TypeError\": TypeError,\n    \"KeyError\": KeyError,\n    \"ZeroDivisionError\": ZeroDivisionError,\n}\n\nUNSUPPORTED_AST_NODES = {\n    ast.Import: \"Import statements (`import ...`) are not supported in the sandbox.\",\n    ast.ImportFrom: \"Import statements (`from ... import ...`) are not supported in the sandbox.\",\n    ast.AsyncFunctionDef: \"Async functions (`async def`) are not supported.\",\n    ast.Await: \"`await` expressions are not supported.\",\n    ast.AsyncFor: \"`async for` loops are not supported.\",\n    ast.AsyncWith: \"`async with` blocks are not supported.\",\n    ast.With: \"`with` context managers (such as file I/O) are not supported.\",\n    ast.Yield: \"Generators (`yield`) are not supported in the beginner tracer.\",\n    ast.YieldFrom: \"`yield from` is not supported.\",\n    ast.Lambda: \"`lambda` functions are not supported; please use a standard `def` function.\",\n    ast.Try: \"`try/except` blocks are not supported in basic mode.\",\n    ast.Global: \"`global` statements are not supported.\",\n    ast.Nonlocal: \"`nonlocal` statements are not supported.\",\n}\n\nFORBIDDEN_CALLS = {\n    \"eval\",\n    \"exec\",\n    \"open\",\n    \"compile\",\n    \"__import__\",\n    \"input\",\n    \"globals\",\n    \"locals\",\n    \"getattr\",\n    \"setattr\",\n    \"delattr\",\n}\n\n\ndef validate_python_support(source_code: str) -> Tuple[bool, Optional[str], Optional[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates syntax and checks whether the code uses only supported beginner constructs.\n    Returns (is_valid, error_message, line_number).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not source_code or not source_code.strip():\n        return False, \"Code editor is empty. Please enter a Python program.\", 1\n\n    try:\n        tree = ast.parse(source_code)\n    except SyntaxError as exc:\n        return False, f\"SyntaxError: {exc.msg}\", exc.lineno or 1\n\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        for node_type, msg in UNSUPPORTED_AST_NODES.items():\n            if isinstance(node, node_type):\n                return False, f\"Unsupported Construct: {msg}\", getattr(node, \"lineno\", 1)\n\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Call) and isinstance(node.func, ast.Name):\n            if node.func.id in FORBIDDEN_CALLS:\n                return (\n                    False,\n                    f\"Restricted Function: `{node.func.id}()` is disabled for security.\",\n                    getattr(node, \"lineno\", 1),\n                )\n\n    return True, None, None\n\n\ndef format_py_val(val: Any) -> str:\n    if isinstance(val, str):\n        return repr(val)\n    if isinstance(val, (int, float, bool, list, dict, tuple, set)) or val is None:\n        return repr(val)\n    return f\"<{type(val).__name__} instance>\"\n\n\ndef get_py_type(val: Any) -> str:\n    if val is None:\n        return \"NoneType\"\n    return type(val).__name__\n\n\nclass MemoryHeapTracker:\n    \"\"\"\n    Deterministic Stack & Heap Memory Reference Tracker (Name -> @Address -> Value)\n    with Visual Garbage Collection (refCount tracking across active stack frames).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.scalar_counter = 0x1000\n        self.container_counter = 0x2000\n        self.scalar_pool: Dict[Tuple[str, str], str] = {}\n        self.container_id_map: Dict[int, str] = {}\n        self.heap_registry: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n\n    def get_or_allocate(self, val: Any, step_idx: int) -> str:\n        py_type = get_py_type(val)\n        val_repr = format_py_val(val)\n\n        if isinstance(val, (list, dict, set, tuple)):\n            obj_id = id(val)\n            if obj_id not in self.container_id_map:\n                addr = f\"@0x{self.container_counter:04X}\"\n                self.container_counter += 0x40\n                self.container_id_map[obj_id] = addr\n            else:\n                addr = self.container_id_map[obj_id]\n\n            self.heap_registry[addr] = {\n                \"address\": addr,\n                \"type\": py_type,\n                \"repr\": val_repr,\n                \"isMutable\": isinstance(val, (list, dict, set)),\n                \"elements\": [format_py_val(x) for x in val] if isinstance(val, (list, tuple)) else None,\n                \"lastTouchedStep\": step_idx,\n            }\n        